{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-uniq","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-uniq","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.md","line":1337,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-uniq","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior-uncond]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-uniq","line":3520,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[strong convexity of the closed ball, reduced to uniqueness alone]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-uniq}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior-uncond}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:4.2}\n  Assume only local uniqueness of minimizing geodesics near $p$ (any two\n  constant-speed distance-realizing geodesics joining the same $q_1,q_2$ within $\\beta_U$ of $p$\n  coincide on $[0,1]$). Then there is $\\beta>0$ such that the \\emph{closed} ball\n  $\\overline{B_\\beta(p)}$ is strongly convex (\\cref{def:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex}). This is\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction} together with\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound}.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  Apply \\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound} to\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction}.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[strong convexity of the closed ball, reduced to uniqueness alone] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d342d322d7374726f6e676c79636f6e7665782d756e6971\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior-uncond\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior-uncond</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch3:4.2</span></span>Assume only local uniqueness of minimizing geodesics near <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> (any two constant-speed distance-realizing geodesics joining the same <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q_1,q_2$\">$q_1,q_2$</span> within <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\beta _U$\">$\\beta _U$</span> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> coincide on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$[0,1]$\">$[0,1]$</span>). Then there is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\beta &gt;0$\">$\\beta &gt;0$</span> such that the <em>closed</em> ball <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\overline{B_\\beta (p)}$\">$\\overline{B_\\beta (p)}$</span> is strongly convex (<a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23def%3Adc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a64632d6368332d342d322d7374726f6e676c79636f6e766578\">section 3</a>). This is <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d342d322d7374726f6e676c79636f6e7665782d726564756374696f6e\">section 3</a> together with <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d342d322d6c6f776572626f756e64\">section 3</a>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p>Apply <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d342d322d6c6f776572626f756e64\">section 3</a> to <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d342d322d7374726f6e676c79636f6e7665782d726564756374696f6e\">section 3</a>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior-uncond","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-eqon-flow-reading","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior-uncond","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior-uncond","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior-uncond"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-4-2","title":"prop:dc-ch3-4-2","label":"prop:dc-ch3-4-2"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-uniq","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-uniq","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[strong convexity of the closed ball, reduced to uniqueness alone]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-uniq}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound, lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior-uncond}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:4.2}\n  Assume only local uniqueness of minimizing geodesics near $p$ (any two\n  constant-speed distance-realizing geodesics joining the same $q_1,q_2$ within $\\beta_U$ of $p$\n  coincide on $[0,1]$). Then there is $\\beta>0$ such that the \\emph{closed} ball\n  $\\overline{B_\\beta(p)}$ is strongly convex (\\cref{def:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex}). This is\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction} together with\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound}.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  Apply \\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound} to\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction}.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior-uncond","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior-uncond","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}